# Copy to server/.env for local settings. Every setting is in src/yjsp_server/config.py.

# Local development: sign in as any email without Georgia Tech or Google, as if GT vouched for it, so a new account
# follows the whitelist (never in production).
YJSP_DEV_AUTH=1
# These emails become admins when they sign in.
YJSP_BOOTSTRAP_ADMINS=you@example.com
# To try Georgia Tech sign-in locally, set the two YJSP_MICROSOFT_ settings below: the Entra app has the redirect
# URI http://localhost:8000/auth/microsoft/callback too.

# Whose site it is (docs/design.md, "The web app"): its short name and the team's, which its pages say, and the
# team's logo, a folder with logo-on-light.png and logo-on-dark.png (with neither, the pages show the site's name).
# YJSP's are the defaults.
# YJSP_SITE_NAME=YJSP
# YJSP_TEAM_NAME=Yellow Jacket Space Program
# YJSP_BRAND_DIR=/data/brand

# The school whose accounts people join with (docs/design.md, "Sign-in and accounts"): what the pages call it, its
# email domains (comma-separated; their subdomains too), and its directory in Microsoft Entra, by its tenant ID.
# Georgia Tech's are the defaults. With no domains, people join only by an admin's invite. Where the school's accounts
# are Google's, Google makes accounts for its addresses too.
# YJSP_SCHOOL_NAME=Georgia Tech
# YJSP_SCHOOL_DOMAINS=gatech.edu
# YJSP_MICROSOFT_TENANT=482198bb-ae7b-4b25-8b7a-6d7f32faa083
# YJSP_GOOGLE_MAKES_ACCOUNTS=0

# Production (see docs/design.md, "Deploying"):
# YJSP_ENV=production
# YJSP_PUBLIC_URL=https://yjsp.example.org
# YJSP_SECRET_KEY=<python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))">
# Georgia Tech sign-in: the Entra app's Application (client) ID, and its client secret's value.
# YJSP_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
# YJSP_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET=...
# YJSP_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=...apps.googleusercontent.com
# YJSP_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=...
# YJSP_DATABASE_URL=sqlite:////data/yjsp.db
# Vault's files (every version of every file, in blobs/). Back it up with the database:
# YJSP_VAULT_DIR=/data/vault
# Read each SolidWorks file's 3D view for Caliper once it's checked in, so it's there when the file's first opened
# (on by default; 0: each is read when someone first opens it):
# YJSP_CALIPER_READ_AHEAD=1
# Yorg's files (uploaded test data, the arrays read from it, saved scripts and models). Back it up too:
# YJSP_YORG_DIR=/data/yorg
# Where the off-site backup (deploy/yjsp-offsite, docs/deploying.md "Backups") writes how it went, for Admin > People:
# YJSP_BACKUP_STATUS=/srv/yjsp/backups/offsite.json
# Where Vault-Setup.exe (CI's vault-setup artifact) is, for the web app's SolidWorks page:
# YJSP_DOWNLOADS_DIR=/data/downloads
# Where the help's docs are (README.md, docs/, and the add-in's README, laid out as in the repository): /help shows them,
# and Claude reads them. The default is this repository; the live server keeps a copy beside the server:
# YJSP_HELP_DIR=/opt/yjsp/app/help

# Claude, in Help in the web app (docs/deploying.md, "Claude"): an Anthropic API key, a secret like the ones above; what
# it may spend each calendar month, from 00:00 UTC on the 1st (the API credits a Claude Max plan includes each month);
# what it may spend in all (credits it has once); and what one person's questions may cost in any 24 hours, in US
# dollars. Without a key and a budget (monthly, in all, or both: unset is none), Help has no Claude. Try it locally with
# a key of your own, and a budget of a few dollars.
# YJSP_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# YJSP_ASSISTANT_MONTHLY_BUDGET=95
# YJSP_ASSISTANT_BUDGET=25
# YJSP_ASSISTANT_DAILY_LIMIT=1
# Which model answers, and how hard it thinks: claude-sonnet-5-5 (the default), claude-haiku-5-5 (about a twentieth of
# the price, and weaker at working out what went wrong), or claude-opus-5-5; low, medium, high (the default), xhigh, or
# max (each slower and dearer than the last).
# YJSP_ASSISTANT_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5
# YJSP_ASSISTANT_EFFORT=high
# The server keeps the help loaded between questions: it reads it again whenever nothing has for 50 minutes, so a
# question hours after the last doesn't pay to have it read in full and kept. About $7 a month around the clock with
# Claude Sonnet 5.5 and the help as it is, counted against the budgets; admins can have it kept only for some hours
# after each question instead (Admin > People). 0 turns it off, whatever they choose.
# YJSP_ASSISTANT_KEEP_WARM=0
# Another address for Anthropic's API, as a gateway's (the tests point it at a stand-in). Unset: Anthropic's own.
# YJSP_ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://gateway.example.org
# Bug reports and feature requests from Help: the owner, who alone approves one, by their email (an admin's); and the
# Claude Code routine approving starts, which builds it: the URL and token of its API trigger, from
# claude.ai/code/routines (docs/deploying.md, "Requests"). The token is a secret. Unset: requests can be sent, looked
# at, and declined, but not approved.
# YJSP_FEEDBACK_APPROVER=owner@gatech.edu
# YJSP_FEEDBACK_ROUTINE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com/v1/claude_code/routines/trig_.../fire
# YJSP_FEEDBACK_ROUTINE_TOKEN=
# Deals: eBay's Browse API, searched each day for what the team wants (docs/deploying.md, "Deals"). A production
# keyset's App ID and Cert ID (a secret); the verification token for eBay's account deletion notifications, which go to
# /api/deals/ebay/account-deletion; when to search, the hour in UTC; and the team's ZIP code, for shipping estimates.
# Unset: no deals.
# YJSP_EBAY_CLIENT_ID=YJSP-Deals-PRD-0123456789-abcdef01
# YJSP_EBAY_CLIENT_SECRET=PRD-...
# YJSP_EBAY_VERIFICATION_TOKEN=
# YJSP_DEALS_HOUR=10
# YJSP_DEALS_ZIP=30332
# Claude says which listings would do, its budgets permitting; 0 leaves it to their words.
# YJSP_DEALS_CLAUDE=1

# The demo (docs/design.md and docs/deploying.md, "The demo"): a server of its own, with made-up data (`yjsp-demo seed`
# makes it), at /demo, for anyone to look around without signing in and no one to change. In the demo's own .env, not
# the site's: YJSP_DEMO=1, where the site passes it to (YJSP_ROOT_PATH=/demo), and its own data's folder. It refuses
# to start with any way to sign in, or with Claude's, eBay's, or a routine's settings.
# YJSP_DEMO=1
# YJSP_ROOT_PATH=/demo
# In the site's .env: where the demo's server is, for the site to pass /demo on to. Unset: no demo.
# YJSP_DEMO_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8200
